# Fingerstyle: p i m a (repertoire plan: st-pima-arpeggios). An original right-hand study in the
# manner of the 19th-century guitar methods. Hold each chord and let the notes ring.
# The thumb (p) plays the root: string 5 for C and Am, string 4 for Dm, string 6 for G7;
# i plays string 3, m string 2, a string 1, eight eighths to the bar.
# Bars 1-8 (C, Am): p i m a p i m a. Bars 9-12 (Dm): p a m i p a m i.
# Bars 13-16 (G7): p i m a m i m i, with p and a plucked together on beat 1 of bars 15 and 16.
# It ends on G7, which leads back to the C of bar 1: go round again.
title: Fingerstyle: p i m a
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original study for the right hand, in the classical style
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 3
tags: classical, fingerstyle, arpeggios, p i m a
tempo: 66
time: 4/4
key: C

track: Arpeggios
role: lead
